#4471 is not one problem. Its old “known, one fix” conclusion is superseded by this review.
Keep the parser and form-hint work separate. Neither issue is fixed by this review.

## Separate tickets

- [Parser: month-first parsing of day-first tenant dates](https://github.com/phhien203/mega-s01e03/issues/1).
  The shared parser treats a tenant's day-first input as month first, swapping the month and day.
  For example, Harbour Dental's report R-41200 says 7 April became 4 July.
- [Booking-v3: misleading MM/DD/YYYY hint](https://github.com/phhien203/mega-s01e03/issues/2).
  Day-first tenants using booking-v3 submit month-first input because the form tells them to;
  its tenant-aware reader then interprets it day first. This requires a hint fix, not just the shared parser fix.
  R-41241 is an Alder Physio form report: 6 August became 8 June.

Counts below come from the exported report data and the actual tenant directory, using `uniqueById`,
`causeOf` and `groupByCause` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`. Do not group by the browser's locale or `intakeTag`.
The table's “not this ticket” marker identifies the wrongly merged cause in the original desk ticket;
it now has the separate GitHub ticket linked above.

