## Change the desk's rule now

Use [the revised triage runbook](/kb/triage/dedupe) and
[decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), which supersedes accepted decision 0001 without editing it.
A matching subject is only a search clue. Check the report body, tenant locale, form version and channel.
Merge only reports with the same supported cause; different causes stay in separate tickets even with identical subjects.
Reports with different subjects can still be duplicates. Unknown tenants or unclear symptoms stay unmerged for investigation.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Next actions and verification

Support desk: route new reports to the matching separate ticket, deduplicate by report ID, and preserve provenance.
Do not wait for a product fix to stop the bad merge rule. Reconcile new arrivals against the live queue before closing anything;
this export cannot tell us how many reports arrived after its cutoff.

Engineering: verify the shared-parser fix using a day-first tenant and an ambiguous date; verify the booking-v3 hint
and parser agree for that tenant. Check day > 12 and month-first control cases too.
Keep the unusual timing reports visible until reproductions confirm their cause.

Support lead: review the live cause counts and weekly received-versus-merged view, rather than equating a bulk merge
with an incident start or treating a fresh review date as proof of correctness.
“Known” is a queue label, not evidence that all reports share a fix.

